-- coa29-sch2-part1.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), 2006 c. 46, SCHEDULE 2 "Specified persons, descriptions of disclosures etc for the
-- purposes of section 948", PART 1 "Specified persons". Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Generated by work/gen_sch2.py (the Schedule's words are
-- copied from the text by script; the short labels are hand-written) and work/build.py (quote lines from srcrefs.py).
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Line numbers are of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- TARGET. The stable `l4` (main) 1.6.110.
--
-- WHAT THIS PART DOES. Section 948(2) (coa21) bars the Takeover Panel from disclosing information about an individual's private affairs or a
-- business without that person's consent; s 948(3)(b) says the bar does not apply to a disclosure "made to a person specified in Part 1 of
-- Schedule 2". Part 1 is that list. The bar itself, its other exceptions (3)(a), (c), (d), and the data protection saving (9) are s 948's.
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the recipient is a person the Part lists; JUST FALSE = the
-- recipient is not one of them (s 948(3)(b) hands the question to this list: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a), a definition handed to a list: when no
-- head in the list holds, JUST FALSE); NOTHING = the answer rests on a meaning the text borrows from another Act, which is not known.

